767	  if (prevStage >= DUNNING_EXHAUSTED) {
768	    // Already out of attempts; this was the extra try granted either by the stored
769	    // suspension time arriving or by `retryDunningNow` after the customer saved a
770	    // new card. Silent — they have already had the final notice, and a second copy
771	    // of it would be noise.
772	    //
773	    // The schedule drops back to the plain calendar deadline (already in the past by
774	    // now), so this attempt CANNOT defer the suspension it precedes. When the admin
775	    // kill switch is off nothing will ever be suspended, so fall back to a daily
776	    // cadence instead — otherwise a 10-minute sweep would attempt the same declining
777	    // card every 10 minutes forever, which is exactly how an issuer starts blocking
778	    // us outright.
